00:24:42.540 --> 00:24:45.150
how do I design an identity
and access management

00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:49.290
policy for GCP depending on
the type of customer that I am?

00:24:49.290 --> 00:24:51.810
And we are getting the
answer from Grace Malison.

00:24:51.810 --> 00:24:54.000
She's one of our
solution architects

00:24:54.000 --> 00:24:56.340
that has put together
some great best practices.

00:24:56.340 --> 00:24:58.590
MARK: Yeah, she's written a
really interesting article

00:24:58.590 --> 00:25:02.000
here, as well as a tutorial,
around the differences

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:04.420
and policies that you might
need versus an enterprise

00:25:04.420 --> 00:25:07.270
customer versus a startup,
maybe sort of like an education

00:25:07.270 --> 00:25:08.220
and training system.

00:25:08.220 --> 00:25:12.170
It's really, really nice looking
at a startup, for example.

00:25:12.170 --> 00:25:13.477
People often wear many hats.

00:25:13.477 --> 00:25:15.560
They have many roles, and
they do a lot of things,

00:25:15.560 --> 00:25:17.500
whereas an enterprise, people
can be much more specialized,

00:25:17.500 --> 00:25:19.833
and how you might want to set
up your policies depending

00:25:19.833 --> 00:25:22.240
on those sort of requirements
you have in your systems.

00:25:22.240 --> 00:25:22.810
MELANIE: Yes.

00:25:22.810 --> 00:25:25.420
We'll definitely include
